{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76g.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Not ready to build as written.** Revision 6 closes the clipping finding. Two gaps remain in what the design can certify before shipping. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:224](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:224) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:227) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Clipping is closed. Contrast is still open.** The browser check walks the quote’s ancestors, so a one-line wrapper with `contain: paint` fails even when Morningstar’s quote wraps normally inside it. The contrast check starts its background lookup one element too high. If “Forecast unavailable” has dark text on its **own** dark background inside a light card, line 228 compares the dark text with the light card. That can pass while the reader sees a blank marker. Start the lookup at the element holding the text. The decisive test is that same marker on a contrasting parent. This matters on the first certification, before any hashes are pinned. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:224](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:224) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:228](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:228) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:261)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **The pin leaves the surrounding HTML uncovered.** For an unchanged, certified template and accepted package data, I found no separate forecast leak or outgoing request path. The data is escaped, source addresses are plain text, and the package checker compares the page byte for byte. But that comparison uses the *current* `render_page`, and the two test hashes cover only the style and script. Changing the static fallback sentence, for example, changes what a reader sees when JavaScript is blocked. Both hashes stay identical, and a newly built package still equals the current renderer. Pin the complete template with its data placeholder intact. A change to the fallback alone should then fail the pin. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:72](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:72) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:79) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:90) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:101](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:101) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167)\n     6\t\n     7\t**Convergence.** These two corrections cover the page first certified and the page later shipped. Further checks for hypothetical CSS changes that would already fail the complete-template pin are optional. This was a read-only design review. The browser acceptance run is still ahead. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:186](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:186)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
