{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'contrast|background|pin(ned)?\\\\b|template|fallback|revision 7|76g|acceptance run' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md\"","aggregated_output":"3:**Status: revision 7, ready per council 76g once its two corrections are in; confirmed in round 76h.**\n5:**Revision 7 answers `codex-r76g.md`:**\n6:- **Contrast starts at the text's own element.** Its background is its own non-transparent `background-color`, or else the nearest\n7:  ancestor's. A marker with dark text on its own dark background inside a light card fails.\n8:- **The whole template is pinned.** `page_template()` is the complete page text with the CSP filled and one data placeholder;\n9:  `render_page` splits it at that placeholder and inserts the escaped data. The test pins the sha256 of `page_template()`, so a\n10:  change to any part of the page, the fallback sentence included, fails the pin until re-certified.\n12:Council 76g judged further checks against hypothetical CSS optional once these are in: a template change already fails the pin.\n18:2. **Contrast.** Every read text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 between its computed colour and its effective background (the\n19:   nearest ancestor with a non-transparent background), in light and in dark. This is WCAG's AA level for body text.\n20:3. **The template is pinned.** The sha256 of `PAGE_STYLE` and `PAGE_SCRIPT` are literals in the tests. The screen check certifies\n21:   that exact template, and any template change fails the tests until it is re-certified by a new screen run and a new format\n25:- The template's stylesheet uses none of `overflow`, `clip`, `text-overflow`, `line-clamp`, `max-height` or `nowrap`.\n34:- the template's stylesheet draws no text (no `content`);\n42:- the dark background is the literal `rgb(15, 20, 13)`.\n50:- the fallback, timer, phone-width and dark-scheme conditions are made observable;\n81:**A visible fallback.** The page starts with the line \"This release page needs JavaScript to show its questions.\" The script removes it\n88:- **`render_page(data_bytes) -> bytes`:** one fixed template, the module constant `PAGE_TEMPLATE`, with the data inserted once.\n97:    connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'`. The two hashes are computed from the template's own script and style,\n114:  and no code the template does not hold.\n140:| The browser blocks the inline script | the fallback line stays visible; nothing else renders, and the page holds no forecast to leak |\n142:| The template changes in a later version | old packages fail `check_package` under the new code by design; a new template is a new format version |\n143:| A dark scheme and a phone width | checked in §6: at 390 px wide the page has no horizontal scroll; with the dark scheme emulated, the body's background is the dark token |\n160:| `release_check.py` pins `hivemind-release/1`; its helpers that forge data refresh only the data hash | the pin becomes `/2`. The forging helpers also regenerate `index.html = render_page(forged data)` and its hash, so a forged forecast still reaches the store comparison and is refused there, with its exact reason |\n172:   - The template's script contains none of the listed APIs, and no `createElement('a')`, `href` or `src`.\n176:   - The sha256 of `page_template()` (the whole page with its one data placeholder) equals a literal written in the test after the\n236:- **Readable.** Each kept text's contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1, computed (WCAG relative luminance) between its element's computed\n237:  `color` and the first non-transparent `background-color` found from that element itself upward, the page canvas if none. This is checked in light and in\n272:- **unreadable marker:** in dark, the marker drawn in `--ink` on an `--ink` background (`color` set to `rgb(15, 20, 13)` through the\n273:  script's inline style) fails the contrast rule, although its text, box and opacity pass;\n274:- **marker on its own background:** in light, the marker given dark text on its own dark background (`color` and `background` both\n275:  `rgb(15, 20, 13)`) inside the light card fails the contrast rule.\n299:- With `Emulation.setEmulatedMedia` `prefers-color-scheme: dark`, the body's computed background is exactly `rgb(15, 20, 13)` (the\n303:- at most 3 s for the `old-1` page in headless Chrome, from `Page.navigate` until the full list is visible: the fallback line is\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | sed -n '1,53p;78,115p;161,191p;232,240p;267,278p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | sed -n '1,53p;78,115p;161,191p;232,240p;267,278p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release, slice 2: the reader's page (design for council round 76)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: revision 7, ready per council 76g once its two corrections are in; confirmed in round 76h.**\n     4\t\n     5\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r76g.md`:**\n     6\t- **Contrast starts at the text's own element.** Its background is its own non-transparent `background-color`, or else the nearest\n     7\t  ancestor's. A marker with dark text on its own dark background inside a light card fails.\n     8\t- **The whole template is pinned.** `page_template()` is the complete page text with the CSP filled and one data placeholder;\n     9\t  `render_page` splits it at that placeholder and inserts the escaped data. The test pins the sha256 of `page_template()`, so a\n    10\t  change to any part of the page, the fallback sentence included, fails the pin until re-certified.\n    11\t\n    12\tCouncil 76g judged further checks against hypothetical CSS optional once these are in: a template change already fails the pin.\n    13\t\n    14\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r76f.md` with general rules instead of one patch per trick** (AGENTS §1: \"certify what the reader can\n    15\tread\" drew a new finding in 76c, 76d and 76f):\n    16\t1. **No clipping ancestor.** No element between a read text and `body` may clip it: computed `overflow-x` or `overflow-y` other than\n    17\t   `visible`, `contain` holding `paint`, `strict` or `content`, or `clip-path` other than `none`.\n    18\t2. **Contrast.** Every read text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 between its computed colour and its effective background (the\n    19\t   nearest ancestor with a non-transparent background), in light and in dark. This is WCAG's AA level for body text.\n    20\t3. **The template is pinned.** The sha256 of `PAGE_STYLE` and `PAGE_SCRIPT` are literals in the tests. The screen check certifies\n    21\t   that exact template, and any template change fails the tests until it is re-certified by a new screen run and a new format\n    22\t   version.\n    23\t\n    24\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r76d.md`:** no text may be clipped.\n    25\t- The template's stylesheet uses none of `overflow`, `clip`, `text-overflow`, `line-clamp`, `max-height` or `nowrap`.\n    26\t- In the browser, every block element holding read text shows all of it. This is checked at desktop width and at 390 px, with the\n    27\t  stored Morningstar entry as the test.\n    28\t- A clipping copy is added as a negative page.\n    29\t\n    30\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r76c.md`:**\n    31\t- the screen check compares the whole page's visible text, header and every card, with a frozen list; any text outside a known place\n    32\t  fails;\n    33\t- visibility is one test, `checkVisibility` with opacity and visibility, for the evidence and for the timer;\n    34\t- the template's stylesheet draws no text (no `content`);\n    35\t- a sibling forecast line and a fully transparent list are added as negative pages.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r76b.md`:**\n    38\t- the screen check compares every visible text of each checked card with a frozen list, in order and grouped by evidence, so an\n    39\t  extra line fails;\n    40\t- each dated card is frozen from its own dated package;\n    41\t- the timer stops when the list is visible;\n    42\t- the dark background is the literal `rgb(15, 20, 13)`.\n    43\t\n    44\tRevision 2 answered `codex-r76.md`:\n    45\t- source addresses are plain text, never links;\n    46\t- the escaping is written out as literal JSON escapes, with the charset and the CSP first in the file;\n    47\t- the format-1 checks are updated, and a lone page-hash error has its own test;\n    48\t- the screen check compares the expanded `v8` card with frozen expected entries;\n    49\t- the fetch mutant keeps its script running and must name `connect-src` and its destination;\n    50\t- the fallback, timer, phone-width and dark-scheme conditions are made observable;\n    51\t- the text filter is dropped. Slice 1 is built and accepted (D759: `RELEASE-BUILD.md` revision 11,\n    52\t`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`). Council 73 (D758) ordered the exporter first and the reader's screen second. This slice completes D756's\n    53\tscreen check: a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a forecast and history, where only the\n    78\t\n    79\t## 1. What is built\n    80\t\n    81\t**A visible fallback.** The page starts with the line \"This release page needs JavaScript to show its questions.\" The script removes it\n    82\tonce the list is built. A browser that blocks the inline script keeps that line (`<noscript>` would stay hidden there; council\n    83\t76).\n    84\t\n    85\t**In `src/hivemind/release.py`:**\n    86\t- **`FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/2'`.** The data's allow-list (`release-allow-list/1`) is unchanged.\n    87\t- **`PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json', 'index.html'}`.** The manifest's closed set gains `page_sha256`.\n    88\t- **`render_page(data_bytes) -> bytes`:** one fixed template, the module constant `PAGE_TEMPLATE`, with the data inserted once.\n    89\t  - **The data** goes into `<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"release-data\">`, written from the exact `release-data.json` bytes,\n    90\t    with each of these characters replaced by its six-character JSON escape: `<` by `\\u003c`, `>` by `\\u003e`, `&` by `\\u0026`,\n    91\t    U+2028 by `\\u2028`, U+2029 by `\\u2029`. These replacements stay valid JSON and parse back to the same data. The block can then\n    92\t    hold no `</script` and no `<!--`.\n    93\t  - **The file starts** with `<!doctype html>`, then `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, then the CSP `<meta>`, before any style, script or\n    94\t    data.\n    95\t  - **A Content-Security-Policy `<meta>`:**\n    96\t    `default-src 'none'; script-src 'sha256-<inline script>'; style-src 'sha256-<inline style>'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none';\n    97\t    connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'`. The two hashes are computed from the template's own script and style,\n    98\t    so the browser refuses any other script, style or connection.\n    99\t  - **The script** builds the page only with `document.createElement`, `textContent` and `className`. It creates no `<a>` element,\n   100\t    no `href` and no `src`. It never uses `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, `insertAdjacentHTML`, `document.write`, `eval`, `Function`, or any network API\n   101\t    (`fetch`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `WebSocket`, `EventSource`, `navigator.sendBeacon`, `import()`, `Worker`).\n   102\t  - **The style** uses system fonts and inline colour tokens copied from `web/design-system/tokens.css`. It generates no text: no\n   103\t    `content` property anywhere, so every word a reader sees is a text node the screen check can read. It clips no text: none of\n   104\t    `overflow`, `clip`, `text-overflow`, `line-clamp`, `max-height` or `white-space: nowrap`, and long words wrap\n   105\t    (`overflow-wrap: anywhere`). It has a dark scheme under\n   106\t    `prefers-color-scheme: dark`, and it works at phone width.\n   107\t- **`write_package`** also writes `index.html = render_page(data bytes)` and records its sha256.\n   108\t- **`check_package`** also:\n   109\t  - reads `index.html` once through the same folder handle;\n   110\t  - requires its bytes to equal `render_page(the data bytes it read)` exactly;\n   111\t  - requires the manifest's `page_sha256` to match.\n   112\t\n   113\t  A page that differs by one byte from the function of the data is refused. So a page cannot carry anything the data does not hold,\n   114\t  and no code the template does not hold.\n   115\t\n   161\t\n   162\t## 5. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n   163\t\n   164\t1. **Determinism.** `render_page` of the fixture data twice gives the same bytes.\n   165\t2. **Escaping.**\n   166\t   - A fixture quote holding `</script><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>`, an `&` and a U+2028 is embedded with the literal escapes.\n   167\t   - The page bytes hold no `</script` inside the data block and no `<!--`.\n   168\t   - Parsing the block back gives the data unchanged.\n   169\t   - In the browser check (§6), on the fixture page with that evidence expanded, the exact quote is visible as text, and the page has\n   170\t     no `img` element.\n   171\t3. **No network code, no drawn text.**\n   172\t   - The template's script contains none of the listed APIs, and no `createElement('a')`, `href` or `src`.\n   173\t   - Its CSP is exactly the policy above, with the hashes of its own script and style.\n   174\t   - Its stylesheet has no `content` property, and none of `overflow` (as a property name, so `overflow-wrap` is allowed), `clip`,\n   175\t     `clip-path`, `contain`, `text-overflow`, `line-clamp`, `max-height`, `nowrap`, `opacity` or `visibility`.\n   176\t   - The sha256 of `page_template()` (the whole page with its one data placeholder) equals a literal written in the test after the\n   177\t     screen run certifies it. A change to any part of the page fails this until it is re-certified.\n   178\t4. **The package check:**\n   179\t   - a page changed by one byte, with the manifest hash refreshed, is refused with its exact reason;\n   180\t   - a page with `fetch(\"http://127.0.0.1:59999/library\")` added, its CSP hash and manifest hash both updated, is refused, because it\n   181\t     is not `render_page(data)`;\n   182\t   - **a correct page with only `page_sha256` wrong is refused with its exact reason**, which catches a deleted hash check;\n   183\t   - a missing page and a fourth file are each refused;\n   184\t   - all three files are read once through the folder handle, and the page bytes compared are the bytes hashed.\n   185\t5. **Literal identifiers:** `hivemind-release/2` and `release-allow-list/1`, in the tests and the acceptance script.\n   186\t\n   187\t**Mutants:**\n   188\t- `render_page` not escaping `<`;\n   189\t- the script using `innerHTML` for the quote;\n   190\t- a source address rendered as a link;\n   191\t- `check_package` not comparing the page with `render_page`;\n   232\t    its `scrollHeight` at most `clientHeight + 1`.\n   233\t  - No ancestor between it and `body` clips: none has `overflow-x` or `overflow-y` other than `visible`, `contain` holding `paint`,\n   234\t    `strict` or `content`, or `clip-path` other than `none`.\n   235\t  - Any clipped text fails the page, whatever its content.\n   236\t- **Readable.** Each kept text's contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1, computed (WCAG relative luminance) between its element's computed\n   237\t  `color` and the first non-transparent `background-color` found from that element itself upward, the page canvas if none. This is checked in light and in\n   238\t  dark. Any text below the ratio fails the page.\n   239\t- **Where each text goes:** to the header, to a card (by `data-id`), to an evidence group within a card, or else to `other`.\n   240\t  `other` must be empty.\n   267\t  exists;\n   268\t- **clipped:** quotes held to one line (`white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis` added through the script's\n   269\t  inline style on each quote) fail the not-clipped rule at 390 px, although their text is identical;\n   270\t- **clipping wrapper:** each quote placed inside a one-line wrapper (`contain: paint; height: 1.5em`), the quote itself wrapping\n   271\t  normally, fails the clipping-ancestor rule at 390 px;\n   272\t- **unreadable marker:** in dark, the marker drawn in `--ink` on an `--ink` background (`color` set to `rgb(15, 20, 13)` through the\n   273\t  script's inline style) fails the contrast rule, although its text, box and opacity pass;\n   274\t- **marker on its own background:** in light, the marker given dark text on its own dark background (`color` and `background` both\n   275\t  `rgb(15, 20, 13)`) inside the light card fails the contrast rule.\n   276\t\n   277\t**The escaping screen.** The fixture page of test 2, with that evidence expanded, shows the exact quote as text and has no `img`\n   278\telement.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**Ready to build.** Revision 7 closes both 76g findings in the design. Browser acceptance remains ahead.\n\n1. **Contrast lookup — closed.** The check starts at the element holding the text and walks upward only if its background is transparent. The decisive test requires “Forecast unavailable” to fail when its dark text sits on its own dark background inside a light card. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:237](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:237) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:274)\n2. **Whole-page template pin — closed.** The renderer inserts escaped data into the complete template’s single placeholder. After browser certification, the test records the SHA-256 of that template with the placeholder intact. Changing only the fallback sentence therefore fails the test. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:8) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:176)\n\n**Optional.** Further tests for hypothetical CSS changes remain optional because those edits already change the complete template’s hash. [codex-r76g.md:7](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76g.md:7)"}}
